    <div aria-label="Ingredients three and four"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-reason"> <div class="gp-num">3</div> <h3>Black Maca</h3> <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Black Maca" loading="lazy" width="900" height="600"> <span class="gp-dose">Look for ~1000mg</span> <p>Grown above 13,000ft in the Peruvian Andes, taken for centuries for stamina and daytime energy. It doesn't work through the same pathway as the first two, which is exactly why it belongs in the stack rather than instead of it &mdash; you want ingredients that cover different bases, not four versions of the same thing.</p> </div> <div class="gp-reason"> <div class="gp-num">4</div> <h3>Shilajit</h3> <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Shilajit" loading="lazy" width="900" height="600"> <span class="gp-dose">Look for ~200mg, fulvic-acid standardised</span> <p>The Himalayan resin. This is the one most men haven't tried, usually because buying it on its own is a hassle and half the products are low quality. Standardised for fulvic acid, it rounds out the group &mdash; and it's the ingredient that turns a decent stack into a complete one.</p></div> </div></div>
